WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.467 --> 00:00:05.133
-Hey, everybody.
I'm fighting a cold.

00:00:05.133 --> 00:00:09.367
So fair warning, tonight's
pacing will be lethargic.

00:00:12.267 --> 00:00:13.667
I was told in
no uncertain terms

00:00:13.667 --> 00:00:16.234
that you shouldn't drink
your own urine

00:00:16.234 --> 00:00:21.801
if you're in the desert, it will
only dehydrate you faster.

00:00:21.801 --> 00:00:23.501
Worst comes to worst,
they recommend

00:00:23.501 --> 00:00:26.067
a half a glass of Coors Light.

00:00:26.067 --> 00:00:30.234
[ Laughter ]

00:00:30.234 --> 00:00:36.868
We made a joke that
the GOP governs like a Roomba.

00:00:36.868 --> 00:00:38.734
If it bumps into something
it doesn't understand,

00:00:38.734 --> 00:00:40.100
it goes the opposite direction.

00:00:40.100 --> 00:00:43.300
Someone commented

00:00:43.300 --> 00:00:45.133
that Roombas don't turn back
in the opposite direction

00:00:45.133 --> 00:00:46.601
when they hit something.

00:00:46.601 --> 00:00:52.167
That would just result in one
line being cleared in a room.

00:00:52.167 --> 00:00:54.100
No one wants that.

00:00:54.100 --> 00:00:58.033
They bounce around it, trying
to get a sense of the object.

00:00:58.033 --> 00:01:00.834
I don't bring it up
because of that.

00:01:00.834 --> 00:01:03.200
I bring it up because
the very next comment,

00:01:03.200 --> 00:01:06.801
referring to the one
I just read to you was,

00:01:06.801 --> 00:01:10.267
"Oh, look at Richie Rich
over here with his Roomba."

00:01:10.267 --> 00:01:13.167
[ Laughter ]

00:01:17.067 --> 00:01:19.634
That's a sort of
jackal-on-jackal action

00:01:19.634 --> 00:01:23.501
that gets me up in the morning.

00:01:25.567 --> 00:01:29.767
I showed you

00:01:29.767 --> 00:01:32.934
some great M&amp;Ms last week
that were worth $1,000,000 each,

00:01:32.934 --> 00:01:40.167
thanks to M&amp;Ms 1997 Find
the Imposter M&amp;M Campaign.

00:01:40.167 --> 00:01:42.100
Excuse me,

00:01:42.100 --> 00:01:45.567
a few of you said the M&amp;Ms
I showed didn't look gray,

00:01:45.567 --> 00:01:49.701
they looked silver, and well,

00:01:49.701 --> 00:01:54.467
the folks at the Mars Candy
Corporation agreed with you.

00:01:54.467 --> 00:02:01.367
That was an awkward meeting,
to say the least.

00:02:01.367 --> 00:02:04.734
And a real reminder for me

00:02:04.734 --> 00:02:06.501
not to say,
"Do you know who I am?"

00:02:06.501 --> 00:02:09.667
because in that case, they did

00:02:09.667 --> 00:02:12.634
and they didn't care.

00:02:12.634 --> 00:02:15.801
Also, they were very --
they were very rude.

00:02:15.801 --> 00:02:17.534
It was just a bunch --

00:02:17.534 --> 00:02:21.434
You know,
Mars Candy Corporation.

00:02:21.434 --> 00:02:24.801
They're top of the mountain
and they know it.

00:02:24.801 --> 00:02:26.400
You should see
their boardroom --

00:02:26.400 --> 00:02:31.534
all glass, gorgeous, beautiful
suits, Italian tailors.

00:02:31.534 --> 00:02:32.767
And they're just sitting around,

00:02:32.767 --> 00:02:36.267
and then they start
giving me the high hat.

00:02:36.267 --> 00:02:38.634
Here I am, just an honest guy
trying to get

00:02:38.634 --> 00:02:41.033
a million bucks each for
my gray M&amp;Ms.

00:02:41.033 --> 00:02:42.868
And they're saying, "Those
aren't gray, they're silver.

00:02:42.868 --> 00:02:47.033
And also, why is there silver
Sharpie all over your hands?"

00:02:47.033 --> 00:02:50.534
And I'm like, "Um, 'cause I
sign headshots all day long."

00:02:50.534 --> 00:02:51.767
And they say,

00:02:51.767 --> 00:02:54.734
"Who asks you to sign headshots
all day long?"

00:02:54.734 --> 00:02:56.267
And I say, "Anybody who asks."

00:02:56.267 --> 00:02:57.634
And they say,
"Where do they ask you?"

00:02:57.634 --> 00:03:00.701
And I'm like, "Outside 30 Rock,
every day I walk out."

00:03:00.701 --> 00:03:03.067
And one of them said,
"Hey, I'll make you a deal.

00:03:03.067 --> 00:03:05.567
We'll walk there
with you right now,

00:03:05.567 --> 00:03:07.367
and if someone asks you
to sign a headshot,

00:03:07.367 --> 00:03:10.300
we'll give you
the million dollars."

00:03:10.300 --> 00:03:13.100
And I was like,
"I don't want it like that."

00:03:13.100 --> 00:03:15.100
[ Laughter ]

00:03:18.234 --> 00:03:20.000
We always say Trump talks like

00:03:20.000 --> 00:03:23.000
he's holding
a invisible accordion.

00:03:25.367 --> 00:03:28.000
A gentleman wrote and said
it would be more accurate

00:03:28.000 --> 00:03:34.701
to say an invisible concertina,
because accordions have keys

00:03:34.701 --> 00:03:38.968
and a concertina
does not have keys.

00:03:38.968 --> 00:03:40.701
The guy who told me that
was weird...

00:03:42.701 --> 00:03:44.300
...Al Yankovic.

00:03:49.701 --> 00:03:53.300
I said the word comptroller.
It's pronounced "controller."

00:03:53.300 --> 00:03:59.067
And it's true.
Double checked it. Googled it.

00:03:59.067 --> 00:04:01.334
On my computer.

00:04:01.334 --> 00:04:03.067
Con-puter?

00:04:03.067 --> 00:04:05.701
[ Laughter ]

00:04:06.868 --> 00:04:09.467
Biden wasn't at a podium.
He was at a lectern.

00:04:09.467 --> 00:04:11.534
Lectern is easy to remember,
because it's where you stand

00:04:11.534 --> 00:04:15.200
to lecture, and lecture
is easy to remember

00:04:15.200 --> 00:04:17.334
because it's what
jackals do to get off.

00:04:23.968 --> 00:04:30.701
You don't pay for continental
breakfast at a Motel Six.

00:04:30.701 --> 00:04:33.067
Should have said Motel Five.
Bass joke.

00:04:39.701 --> 00:04:44.667
We called Herschel Walker
a vampire enthusiast.

00:04:44.667 --> 00:04:49.701
That's incorrect. He's
a former vampire enthusiast.

00:04:49.701 --> 00:04:52.133
Because he was watching
the movie "Fright Night."

00:04:52.133 --> 00:04:57.133
That's the clip. The whole clip
that made him famous.

00:04:57.133 --> 00:04:59.200
He discovered watching
a horror movie

00:04:59.200 --> 00:05:00.467
that he stumbled upon one night.

00:05:00.467 --> 00:05:02.200
He used to think
vampires are cool,

00:05:02.200 --> 00:05:05.868
but then he discovered that
werewolves can kill vampires.

00:05:05.868 --> 00:05:09.767
Shoemaker, remember
what can kill a werewolf?

00:05:09.767 --> 00:05:11.000
-Half a glass of Coors Light.

00:05:11.000 --> 00:05:14.367
-♪ The right beer now ♪

00:05:14.367 --> 00:05:17.167
[ Laughter ]

00:05:25.634 --> 00:05:27.234
We received --

00:05:27.234 --> 00:05:34.367
I received to the P.O. box,
two wedding invitations.

00:05:34.367 --> 00:05:36.367
Asking, inviting not just me,

00:05:36.367 --> 00:05:38.701
but also Wally
to attend their weddings.

00:05:40.901 --> 00:05:43.434
So to Brianna and Matthew,
Steph and Alex,

00:05:43.434 --> 00:05:47.234
we wish you the best
in your matrimonial endeavor.

00:05:47.234 --> 00:05:48.634
I unfortunately cannot make it,

00:05:48.634 --> 00:05:52.601
and I will not be
sharing the details

00:05:52.601 --> 00:05:54.200
of your wedding with Wally.

00:05:57.234 --> 00:05:59.534
I have been at weddings
with Wally,

00:05:59.534 --> 00:06:03.400
and this has happened
more than once.

00:06:13.567 --> 00:06:15.000
I was hopeful we'd received

00:06:15.000 --> 00:06:16.968
the last of our
Mack Tonight fan art

00:06:16.968 --> 00:06:18.434
because none had arrived
last week.

00:06:18.434 --> 00:06:20.601
But false alarm.

00:06:20.601 --> 00:06:22.434
Guess it was just cloudy.

00:06:27.734 --> 00:06:30.200
That's not a nice way
to use your time.

00:06:33.501 --> 00:06:36.767
I certainly don't care
for the lack of bravery

00:06:36.767 --> 00:06:39.601
I'm showing in the knife's
reflective edge.

00:06:43.400 --> 00:06:46.133
I'm going to show you this one
in part because

00:06:48.868 --> 00:06:54.300
it's a photo of me
on a red carpet,

00:06:54.300 --> 00:06:57.100
but they've replaced me,
Shoemaker.

00:06:57.100 --> 00:07:02.734
So it's my beautiful wife,
Alexi, with this gentleman.

00:07:02.734 --> 00:07:03.934
And I don't know if you can
tell that

00:07:03.934 --> 00:07:07.634
in the reflective glasses
he's wearing,

00:07:07.634 --> 00:07:10.300
that's me crying,
so I'm seeing it.

00:07:12.601 --> 00:07:14.868
Is that the worst part
of the photo?

00:07:14.868 --> 00:07:19.300
No, because this was an event
where my beautiful wife, Alexi,

00:07:19.300 --> 00:07:23.934
was with child, and Jodie,
the artist in question,

00:07:23.934 --> 00:07:27.734
wanted to let me know
whose child it was.

00:07:29.467 --> 00:07:31.567
[ Laughter ]

00:07:36.234 --> 00:07:38.400
Not cool, Jodie.

00:07:46.501 --> 00:07:49.934
Relax. I don't know.

00:07:49.934 --> 00:07:51.067
Oh, okay.

00:07:51.067 --> 00:07:54.634
So this is cool, remember
I was trying to...

00:07:56.701 --> 00:07:58.501
I got a Faberge egg, guys,

00:07:58.501 --> 00:08:02.000
sent to me.

00:08:02.000 --> 00:08:03.601
Pretty cool, right?

00:08:13.968 --> 00:08:16.501
Here at "Late Night,"

00:08:16.501 --> 00:08:20.968
every night I deliver
a monologue made up of jokes

00:08:20.968 --> 00:08:24.334
written by
a diverse team of writers.

00:08:24.334 --> 00:08:26.601
As a result, a lot of jokes
come across my desk

00:08:26.601 --> 00:08:27.801
that are all about animals.

00:08:27.801 --> 00:08:29.734
It's time for "Animal Flubs."

00:08:29.734 --> 00:08:32.234
-♪ Animal Flubs, Animal Flubs ♪

00:08:32.234 --> 00:08:34.767
♪ It's time to take a look
at some Animal Flubs ♪

00:08:34.767 --> 00:08:37.934
♪ From the birds to the bees
to the baby bear cubs ♪

00:08:37.934 --> 00:08:40.767
♪ It's time for Animal Flubs ♪

00:08:40.767 --> 00:08:43.634
-♪ And I know you don't
need to say "baby" ♪

00:08:43.634 --> 00:08:46.701
♪ Before you say "bear cub" ♪

00:08:46.701 --> 00:08:51.968
♪ Because in that case,
"cub" means baby ♪

00:08:51.968 --> 00:08:53.467
♪ But when you're
writing a song ♪

00:08:53.467 --> 00:08:54.968
♪ On a Thursday afternoon ♪

00:08:54.968 --> 00:08:58.067
♪ When you really should be
working on A Closer Look ♪

00:08:58.067 --> 00:09:01.033
♪ Sometimes your guy
and I cut a few corners ♪

00:09:01.033 --> 00:09:04.200
♪ In order to make
the rhyme scheme work ♪

00:09:04.200 --> 00:09:06.667
-♪ Animal Flubs, Animal Flubs ♪

00:09:06.667 --> 00:09:09.300
♪ I hope you're all ready
for some Animal Flubs ♪

00:09:09.300 --> 00:09:12.400
♪ Call all your pals,
buddies, and buds ♪

00:09:12.400 --> 00:09:14.667
♪ It's time for Animal Flubs ♪

00:09:14.667 --> 00:09:17.634
-♪ And I hope you enjoy
the new voices ♪

00:09:17.634 --> 00:09:20.000
♪ We added to this song ♪

00:09:20.000 --> 00:09:25.267
♪ Because a bunch of you
were unhappy ♪

00:09:25.267 --> 00:09:28.167
♪ So if you're sitting there
now upset at the fact ♪

00:09:28.167 --> 00:09:30.868
♪ That we added a verse
to an overlong song ♪

00:09:30.868 --> 00:09:33.601
♪ Then may we recommend
that you take it up with ♪

00:09:33.601 --> 00:09:35.167
♪ The [bleep] who couldn't just
enjoy a nice thing ♪

00:09:35.167 --> 00:09:36.567
-Enjoy a nice thing.

00:09:36.567 --> 00:09:39.534
-♪ Animal Flubs, Animal Flubs ♪

00:09:39.534 --> 00:09:42.067
♪ I hope you're all ready
for some Animal Flubs ♪

00:09:42.067 --> 00:09:44.834
-♪ Pencil us in for
Best Emmy Song snub ♪

00:09:44.834 --> 00:09:47.667
-♪ It's time for Animal Flubs ♪

00:09:47.667 --> 00:09:49.767
-♪ F ♪

00:09:49.767 --> 00:09:51.601
-♪ L ♪

00:09:51.601 --> 00:09:52.901
-♪ U ♪

00:09:52.901 --> 00:09:55.067
-♪ B ♪

00:09:55.067 --> 00:09:56.701
-♪ S ♪

00:09:56.701 --> 00:10:00.300
-♪ Are the letters ♪

00:10:00.300 --> 00:10:03.868
♪ Used ♪

00:10:03.868 --> 00:10:06.968
♪ To spell "flubs" ♪

00:10:06.968 --> 00:10:08.868
♪ Animal Flubs ♪

00:10:12.567 --> 00:10:15.000
Sorry.

00:10:15.000 --> 00:10:16.167
I thought I had more time.

00:10:16.167 --> 00:10:18.701
[ Laughter ]

00:10:21.367 --> 00:10:26.634
It's e-"mew," not e-"mu."

00:10:26.634 --> 00:10:28.434
It's quokka, not a "quo"-kka.

00:10:28.434 --> 00:10:31.200
A koala baby isn't a cub,
it's a joey,

00:10:31.200 --> 00:10:35.901
because a koala
isn't a bear, it's a marsupial.

00:10:35.901 --> 00:10:40.167
I said we showed a dairy cow
instead of a beef cow

00:10:40.167 --> 00:10:44.601
when we were talking about
the price of beef.

00:10:44.601 --> 00:10:46.567
And someone wrote
that was okay, adding,

00:10:46.567 --> 00:10:49.601
"What do people think happens
to dairy cows

00:10:49.601 --> 00:10:52.734
once the milk production
falls too low?"

00:10:52.734 --> 00:10:56.701
More importantly, what do
the dairy cows think happens?

00:10:56.701 --> 00:11:00.801
"Well,
that's the end of my milk.

00:11:00.801 --> 00:11:03.267
Now I retire to Paris."

00:11:03.267 --> 00:11:05.467
[ Laughter ]

00:11:05.467 --> 00:11:07.667
"That's right, Betsy.
That's right.

00:11:07.667 --> 00:11:12.267
I just need you
to stop by the shed,

00:11:12.267 --> 00:11:13.868
sign some papers."

00:11:13.868 --> 00:11:16.334
[ Laughter ]

00:11:16.334 --> 00:11:18.100
Oh, we said
the Son of Sam's dog

00:11:18.100 --> 00:11:19.934
told him
to go on a killing spree.

00:11:19.934 --> 00:11:21.834
It was his neighbor's dog.

00:11:21.834 --> 00:11:24.267
The Son of Sam's dog
was the one who famously said,

00:11:24.267 --> 00:11:25.868
"Don't listen to him."

00:11:28.400 --> 00:11:33.934
He later recanted that the dog
told him to do it in prison,

00:11:33.934 --> 00:11:36.234
which of course
means the dog got to him.

00:11:40.501 --> 00:11:42.100
Someone said in response
to "Animal Flubs,"

00:11:42.100 --> 00:11:43.467
"'Corrections' jumped the shark

00:11:43.467 --> 00:11:45.567
when they started doing
pre-planned bits."

00:11:45.567 --> 00:11:48.300
You're making "pre"
do a lot of work there.

00:11:54.000 --> 00:11:55.934
Someone said based
on the opening package

00:11:55.934 --> 00:11:58.400
of "Animal Flubs,"

00:11:58.400 --> 00:12:01.968
"You have no idea how animals'
jaws or beaks work."

00:12:05.367 --> 00:12:10.834
Well, pal, you've got no idea
how a graphic department works.

00:12:10.834 --> 00:12:12.400
Last week, to get this
done on time,

00:12:12.400 --> 00:12:13.467
when the show was over,

00:12:13.467 --> 00:12:17.367
we had to put
Tara Donnelly on oxygen.

00:12:17.367 --> 00:12:18.834
Okay?

00:12:18.834 --> 00:12:21.033
What do you think I was going
to do at the end of the show?

00:12:21.033 --> 00:12:22.400
Head on down
to the graphics room

00:12:22.400 --> 00:12:24.701
with a big old book
of animal anatomy,

00:12:24.701 --> 00:12:27.901
giving her a hard time?

00:12:27.901 --> 00:12:29.834
"Tara, take your mask off.

00:12:32.834 --> 00:12:35.133
I don't need her to breathe.
I need her to listen."

00:12:38.634 --> 00:12:41.000
You can still go to jail
if you kill a bald eagle.

00:12:41.000 --> 00:12:42.601
Sorry if I got your hopes up.

00:12:47.634 --> 00:12:48.901
This has been "Animal Flubs."

00:12:48.901 --> 00:12:49.901
-[ Shriek ]

00:12:49.901 --> 00:12:50.801
-Seven days.

